  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mhuri/Imuli II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zimbabwe):  USAID&apos;s Improving Maternal, Newborn and Child Health (MNCH) mechanism helps strengthen the capacity of the national health system to deliver quality services leading to better maternal and newborn health outcomes. With FY 2024 funds, the Mhuri/Imuli II activity will reduce institutional maternal and perinatal mortality rates by 10 percent over a five-year period in selected USG-supported facilities..The activity will:.Provide financial, logistical and operational resources to national, provincial, district and facility levels to enhance policy updates, guidelines, protocols and skills to provide good quality clinical interventions that save lives of mothers, unborn babies, and newborns..Train, improve knowledge and facilitate skills transfer to healthcare workers improving requisite skills that prevent deaths..Work with MoHCC to review the numbers, types and locations of health workers involved in MNCH service delivery and help in planning for their retention in their locations..Improve healthcare worker availability through better planning, management and reviewing how MNCH services are provided..Work with MoHCC at provincial and district levels to identify and pilot initiatives that will help improve working conditions for health workers..Strengthen knowledge and skills for the processes of ordering, maintaining, and distributing stocks of drugs, medical supplies, consumables and equipment needed in providing MNH services..Train, coach and mentor MoHCC colleagues in the collection, cleaning and analysis of commodities and equipment data ensuring the few supplies available are used efficiently..Support health district and local facilities to employ more effective and efficient methods of managing their MNCH commodities and equipment...</narrative>
  </description>
